        "minor": 0,
        "suggestion": 0
      },
      "summary": "The ACR private endpoint assertion now checks that the endpoint targets the ACR resource. The output checks still allow an opaque credential to pass when exposed through a local.",
      "findingList": [
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "file": "infra/terraform/tests/release-identity.tftest.hcl",
          "line": 423,
          "message": "The output check can miss an opaque credential exposed through a local reference. Inspect the resolved output expression or otherwise make this case fail.",
          "confidence": 0.91,
          "category": "security",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "The new source check scans output blocks for credential-related text but does not inspect locals referenced by those blocks. The evaluated-value check can miss opaque credentials.",
            "failureScenario": "If output.model_endpoint is changed to local.model_endpoint and that local resolves to azurerm_storage_account.demo.primary_access_key, the output block contains no matched credential term and the evaluated key may contain none either. The test passes while exposing a storage key, leaving AC RELEASE-ID-04 unenforced (OWASP A02:2025 Security Misconfiguration)."
          }
        }
      ]
    }
